1
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:11,120
Try to lighten up and let it go.

2
00:00:20,140 --> 00:00:24,280
Anyone without money, come to my place.

3
00:00:24,280 --> 00:00:28,980
I've got none either, so don't worry.

4
00:00:28,980 --> 00:00:32,820
Look at the blue sky.

5
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:36,300
White clouds.

6
00:00:37,720 --> 00:00:42,840
Somehow, it'll all work out.

7
00:00:55,860 --> 00:00:59,940
Anyone without a job, come to my place.

8
00:01:00,580 --> 00:01:04,580
I've got none either, so don't worry.

9
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:43,780
Hashutsujo Onsen, what a nice bath

10
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:50,820
So hot, so hot!

11
00:01:50,820 --> 00:01:55,360
Look, heat haze is rising off the road,
and the whole town looks warped.

12
00:01:55,360 --> 00:01:57,920
It's like we're in a desert

13
00:01:57,920 --> 00:02:00,680
"Tokyo Desert" is a fitting name for it.

14
00:02:06,740 --> 00:02:08,460
It's so hot I'm going to die.

15
00:02:10,940 --> 00:02:13,160
Found an oasis in the desert!

16
00:02:13,160 --> 00:02:15,800
Let's take a bath, Nakagawa.

17
00:02:16,880 --> 00:02:19,300
But the police box is right over there.

18
00:02:20,240 --> 00:02:21,120
Senpai.

19
00:02:21,940 --> 00:02:24,860
Being first in the bath at
a place like this is the best.

20
00:02:31,760 --> 00:02:32,580
Excuse me.

21
00:02:33,050 --> 00:02:34,260
I'm parched, I'm parched.

22
00:02:34,260 --> 00:02:36,240
Granny, I'll leave it here.

23
00:02:36,240 --> 00:02:40,660
Phew, you really are a child.

24
00:02:44,960 --> 00:02:45,980
Yahoo!

25
00:02:48,820 --> 00:02:49,660
Puu-zuu.

26
00:02:50,380 --> 00:02:51,960
This is the best, bro.

27
00:02:56,020 --> 00:02:59,040
What an unusual painting.
Is that Mt. Fuji in autumn foliage?

28
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:02,360
Because the name is Momiji, you know.

29
00:03:02,360 --> 00:03:04,820
By the way, the owner's name is Tsurutarō.

30
00:03:04,820 --> 00:03:05,760
The men's bath is...

31
00:03:05,760 --> 00:03:07,840
Crap! It's coming out! Nakagawa!

32
00:03:09,200 --> 00:03:11,380
What's wrong, senpai? All of a sudden?

33
00:03:11,840 --> 00:03:13,800
The maple painting is the women's bath.

34
00:03:13,800 --> 00:03:16,400
The men's bath has the
crane on the hill in front!

35
00:03:16,600 --> 00:03:17,140
Huh? Huh?

36
00:03:19,920 --> 00:03:22,640
Honestly,
mixing up the men's and women's noren

37
00:03:22,640 --> 00:03:23,920
like that!

38
00:03:23,920 --> 00:03:25,120
That gave me a cold sweat.

39
00:03:25,600 --> 00:03:26,560
Sorry about that.

40
00:03:27,100 --> 00:03:29,200
Business has been really slow lately.

41
00:03:30,680 --> 00:03:31,960
We've gotten a bit careless.

42
00:03:31,960 --> 00:03:35,620
Come to think of it, the bathhouse on
4-chome turned into a supermarket, didn't it?

43
00:03:36,140 --> 00:03:40,400
We've been talking about
calling it quits soon, too.

44
00:03:40,400 --> 00:03:43,320
The young ones want to turn
it into an apartment building,

45
00:03:43,320 --> 00:03:45,020
my son and his wife, you see.

46
00:03:45,540 --> 00:03:49,460
Well, with the economy like this, I can't really
say they should take over the bathhouse as it is.

47
00:03:52,260 --> 00:03:55,260
In the old days, teachers and
students would meet face to face,

48
00:03:56,280 --> 00:03:58,300
and shogi friends would form their circles.

49
00:03:59,200 --> 00:04:01,380
The public bath used to be a place for socializing,
you know.

50
00:04:01,380 --> 00:04:03,700
But that's just the way of the times.

51
00:04:03,700 --> 00:04:07,100
Right, Granny, I'll have a coffee milk.

52
00:04:09,760 --> 00:04:13,840
Sorry, Ryo-san, we don't stock coffee milk.

53
00:04:13,840 --> 00:04:16,800
Young people only ever drink
mineral water these days.

54
00:04:16,800 --> 00:04:19,460
Mineral water after a bath

55
00:04:19,920 --> 00:04:23,480
Another bathhouse pleasure gone, I see.

56
00:04:25,480 --> 00:04:28,760
Now that you mention it,
I drink mineral water too.

57
00:04:28,760 --> 00:04:29,720
Me too.

58
00:04:30,400 --> 00:04:32,520
Reiko aside, even Terai?

59
00:04:32,520 --> 00:04:36,860
At home, we even use it when
making barley tea or coffee.

60
00:04:36,860 --> 00:04:41,100
What, mineral water even
for barley tea and coffee?

61
00:04:41,700 --> 00:04:43,100
It's the same at the police box.

62
00:04:46,660 --> 00:04:50,400
This tastes no different from something made with tap water,
you know.

63
00:04:50,820 --> 00:04:54,320
But only Ryo-chan's was made with tap water.

64
00:04:54,320 --> 00:04:57,480
Why is it only mine that's tap water?

65
00:04:57,480 --> 00:05:00,980
I thought Ryo-chan liked
the taste of tap water.

66
00:05:01,660 --> 00:05:06,720
That's right, you always stick your face under the faucet and drink it, saying
"So good, so good!"

67
00:05:06,720 --> 00:05:09,900
Even so,
there's no need to make only mine tap water.

68
00:05:09,900 --> 00:05:15,080
Then you should have said from the
start that you wanted mineral water.

69
00:05:15,080 --> 00:05:19,360
A personal mineral water bottle

70
00:05:20,400 --> 00:05:24,480
These days, people even carry mineral
water plastic bottles when they go out.

71
00:05:25,620 --> 00:05:27,580
Everyone's jumping on the
mineral water bandwagon.

72
00:05:27,580 --> 00:05:29,160
Mineral water

73
00:05:41,920 --> 00:05:42,780
Mister

74
00:05:49,180 --> 00:05:52,980
This oasis isn't mineral water.

75
00:05:55,760 --> 00:05:59,120
Even if you find an oasis
while wandering the desert,

76
00:05:59,120 --> 00:06:03,120
and the guy dies saying
he'll only drink mineral water,

77
00:06:03,120 --> 00:06:04,940
I'll respect him for the rest of my life.

78
00:06:06,840 --> 00:06:08,960
That's an extreme example.

79
00:06:08,960 --> 00:06:10,880
Yeah, no matter what, come on.

80
00:06:12,840 --> 00:06:14,180
How much is one bottle?

81
00:06:14,580 --> 00:06:16,440
Well, I'd say about 200 yen.

82
00:06:17,100 --> 00:06:19,193
200 yen? So that means,

83
00:06:19,243 --> 00:06:22,700
if everyone in Japan drank one bottle each,

84
00:06:22,750 --> 00:06:23,920
20 billion yen?

85
00:06:24,600 --> 00:06:27,850
Wait. If I strike a well with mineral water,

86
00:06:27,900 --> 00:06:28,800
the water's free for the taking.

87
00:06:29,140 --> 00:06:32,180
If I sell it, every last yen
of profit comes straight to me.

88
00:06:32,500 --> 00:06:34,880
That means 20 billion yen comes rolling in!

89
00:06:35,560 --> 00:06:38,360
Alright! Let's give it a go!

90
00:06:47,300 --> 00:06:48,760
He's started something again.

91
00:06:49,220 --> 00:06:52,740
He's going to dig up groundwater
he can sell as mineral water.

92
00:06:52,740 --> 00:06:53,420
I bet he is.

93
00:06:53,420 --> 00:06:56,140
Ryo-san,
you can't just dig there without permission.

94
00:06:56,140 --> 00:06:58,880
Don't come crying to me when the
Chief catches you and scolds you.

95
00:07:01,820 --> 00:07:03,280
He's not listening at all.

96
00:07:03,280 --> 00:07:07,260
When money's involved, Ryo-chan's
concentration is unmatched in the whole world.

97
00:07:19,120 --> 00:07:21,740
Well then, Dad and Mom,
this is fine with you both, right?

98
00:07:21,740 --> 00:07:24,580
I'll leave everything to you.

99
00:07:25,520 --> 00:07:30,860
It's a bit sad to think we'll
never see this chimney again, though.

100
00:07:31,280 --> 00:07:33,680
It would be different if we
opened a hot spring, though.

101
00:07:34,640 --> 00:07:36,160
It's not that easy.

102
00:07:37,620 --> 00:07:40,120
Hot spring

103
00:07:48,740 --> 00:07:52,240
Gush out, gush out, mineral water!

104
00:07:52,240 --> 00:07:54,660
Gush out, gush out, mineral water!

105
00:07:59,740 --> 00:08:01,780
What, he's digging a well?

106
00:08:01,780 --> 00:08:04,060
Yeah, right beside that police box...

107
00:08:04,060 --> 00:08:06,980
Apparently he plans to sell
groundwater as mineral water.

108
00:08:07,600 --> 00:08:08,960
That idiot!

109
00:08:10,440 --> 00:08:11,980
Hey, Ryotsu!

110
00:08:15,480 --> 00:08:17,700
Did he dig this hole with just one shovel?

111
00:08:17,700 --> 00:08:21,140
He's digging by hand, so it must be
at least 100 meters deep, I'd guess.

112
00:08:22,400 --> 00:08:24,920
Hey, Ryotsu, can you hear me?

113
00:08:27,540 --> 00:08:29,780
Get out here right now, you idiot!

114
00:08:34,820 --> 00:08:36,440
Ugh, what is it now? So noisy.

115
00:08:36,920 --> 00:08:40,040
If you keep dawdling,
I'll bury you alive right here!

116
00:08:43,900 --> 00:08:45,260
Well, what did you just say?

117
00:08:45,960 --> 00:08:46,740
Oh no!

118
00:08:54,140 --> 00:08:55,140
What could it be?

119
00:08:56,040 --> 00:08:57,360
Hey, Ryo-chan.

120
00:08:57,360 --> 00:08:58,500
Whoa!

121
00:08:58,500 --> 00:09:00,300
Whoa!

122
00:09:00,300 --> 00:09:03,280
Whoa!

123
00:09:03,280 --> 00:09:04,860
Whoa!

124
00:09:04,860 --> 00:09:06,320
Whoa!

125
00:09:06,320 --> 00:09:07,260
Whoa!

126
00:09:08,680 --> 00:09:10,020
Ryo-chan!

127
00:09:10,020 --> 00:09:11,740
Ow!

128
00:09:11,740 --> 00:09:15,220
Ryo-chan, this is...

129
00:09:15,220 --> 00:09:17,280
It's not water, it's hot water.

130
00:09:17,280 --> 00:09:18,960
I struck a hot spring!

131
00:09:18,960 --> 00:09:20,320
No way!

132
00:09:20,320 --> 00:09:21,520
Ouch, it's hot!

133
00:09:23,820 --> 00:09:25,420
I did it!

134
00:09:32,200 --> 00:09:34,140
I did it, Kankichi Ryotsu!

135
00:09:35,400 --> 00:09:38,040
This will make more
money than mineral water!

136
00:09:47,100 --> 00:09:50,640
I never expected the hot spring
Ryotsu dug up to be this popular.

137
00:09:50,640 --> 00:09:56,640
Yes, he says he's serving the
local residents at a special price.

138
00:09:57,360 --> 00:10:02,100
Alright, line up, line up! The admission
fee is the only thing you need to pay, okay?

139
00:10:02,100 --> 00:10:07,200
Chief! Thanks to you,
the residents are loving it.

140
00:10:07,200 --> 00:10:09,100
The Police Box Hot Spring is...

141
00:10:09,100 --> 00:10:14,320
Ryotsu, you're really only charging the
admission fee and nothing else, right?

142
00:10:14,840 --> 00:10:18,800
Of course.
It's purely a service for the residents.

143
00:10:19,640 --> 00:10:21,800
I'm going to take a look inside.

144
00:10:21,800 --> 00:10:24,200
Well

145
00:10:24,780 --> 00:10:28,040
What's wrong? Do you have something to hide?

146
00:10:28,040 --> 00:10:29,960
That's not true at all.

147
00:10:29,960 --> 00:10:33,860
Please, Chief and Chief Ohara,
do come in and enjoy the hot spring.

148
00:10:34,520 --> 00:10:37,960
Come right in, two adults this way!

149
00:10:38,880 --> 00:10:41,320
Welcome!

150
00:10:42,680 --> 00:10:45,240
Nakagawa and Reiko are working here too

151
00:10:45,860 --> 00:10:46,260
Yes.

152
00:10:46,260 --> 00:10:49,760
When it's called a service for residents,
we can't really say no.

153
00:10:54,480 --> 00:10:57,540
How about it? We've put handsome men
and beautiful women at the front desk.

154
00:10:57,540 --> 00:11:00,020
We've made it easy for the residents to use.

155
00:11:01,200 --> 00:11:04,260
From the outside,
it looks just like an ordinary public bath.

156
00:11:05,080 --> 00:11:06,960
Yes, yes, Chief and Chief Ohara.

157
00:11:08,100 --> 00:11:10,120
The men's bath is this way, you know.

158
00:11:19,100 --> 00:11:21,400
An outdoor bath

159
00:11:21,400 --> 00:11:22,760
It's bigger than I expected.

160
00:11:22,760 --> 00:11:26,300
After all,
it's 100% natural hot spring water.

161
00:11:26,300 --> 00:11:29,260
Then, let me wash your backs first.

162
00:11:30,900 --> 00:11:31,820
Hey!

163
00:11:32,320 --> 00:11:35,480
Wash these two gentlemen's backs first.

164
00:11:36,020 --> 00:11:36,980
Here goes!

165
00:11:36,980 --> 00:11:38,220
You're still doing this?

166
00:11:39,280 --> 00:11:40,240
Whoa!

167
00:11:42,960 --> 00:11:43,800
Uh-oh!

168
00:11:43,800 --> 00:11:45,620
It's Chief Ohara and the Chief.

169
00:11:45,620 --> 00:11:47,940
Nice, special service!

170
00:11:49,060 --> 00:11:50,660
Don't you dare take any tips, okay?

171
00:12:19,240 --> 00:12:21,540
Listen,
just keep up the business in the break room.

172
00:12:23,540 --> 00:12:24,980
Well, this is quite something.

173
00:12:24,980 --> 00:12:27,740
Hot springs really are nice, aren't they?

174
00:12:28,620 --> 00:12:32,540
Chief, the massage is ready.
Please, this way.

175
00:12:32,540 --> 00:12:34,780
You even have massage service?

176
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:40,960
It really takes the fatigue away,
doesn't it?

177
00:12:40,960 --> 00:12:44,960
Right? This is just right
for an era that craves healing.

178
00:12:44,960 --> 00:12:46,480
It's the police box hot spring.

179
00:12:46,480 --> 00:12:49,640
The police box hot spring is
an oasis for the common people.

180
00:12:54,640 --> 00:12:57,780
As long as we keep these two in line,
we've got it made.

181
00:12:57,780 --> 00:12:59,260
We're going to rake in the money!

182
00:13:25,420 --> 00:13:26,680
So this is it, then.

183
00:13:26,680 --> 00:13:27,300
Yes.

184
00:13:34,740 --> 00:13:37,180
Grandma, I'm sorry.

185
00:13:37,180 --> 00:13:40,040
I heard the bathhouse here is gone.

186
00:13:41,740 --> 00:13:44,900
Grandma, you used to bathe in this big bath here,
didn't you?

187
00:13:46,480 --> 00:13:49,180
Yes, I did. But there's no help for it.

188
00:13:56,300 --> 00:14:01,360
There are still people who look forward to our bath,
like those over there.

189
00:14:09,960 --> 00:14:13,360
Massage fees, hot spring buns,
and hot spring eggs.

190
00:14:13,360 --> 00:14:16,820
Plus the sales from the
beer and edamame stand.

191
00:14:16,820 --> 00:14:20,140
We're not making as much
profit as I expected.

192
00:14:20,140 --> 00:14:22,060
Massage work is really exhausting, you know.

193
00:14:22,060 --> 00:14:23,940
You are going to pay us
our wages properly, right?

194
00:14:24,360 --> 00:14:25,440
Don't worry, don't worry.

195
00:14:25,440 --> 00:14:28,480
I'm steadily preparing my next scheme.

196
00:14:28,480 --> 00:14:29,900
Your next scheme?

197
00:14:37,040 --> 00:14:40,720
Behold! The New Hashutsujo Hot Spring.
Here's the full layout!

198
00:14:42,120 --> 00:14:44,940
First, you pass through the main gate,
the Ote-mon,

199
00:14:45,620 --> 00:14:48,300
then ride this bath palanquin to get around.

200
00:14:48,300 --> 00:14:50,360
In the Ninomaru, there's the Neon Bath,

201
00:14:50,360 --> 00:14:52,220
in the East Circle, the Bubble Bath,

202
00:14:52,220 --> 00:14:54,180
in the Donjon, the Lord's Bath,

203
00:14:54,180 --> 00:14:56,180
and in the Honmaru, the Electric Bath.

204
00:14:56,180 --> 00:14:57,860
In the West Circle, the Hinoki Bath,

205
00:14:57,860 --> 00:14:59,980
and in the Third Circle, the Mineral Bath.

206
00:15:00,520 --> 00:15:02,280
And here, the Leisure Bath,

207
00:15:02,680 --> 00:15:06,340
lets you soak in the hot spring while
enjoying a panorama of greater Tokyo.

208
00:15:06,980 --> 00:15:14,080
We'll also build a freezing bath that gives you goosebumps in the buff,
and a hot water slider bath for thrills.

209
00:15:14,540 --> 00:15:18,960
With seven baths and attractions,
it's fun for everyone from adults to kids.

210
00:15:18,960 --> 00:15:22,840
A true dream hot spring, Dejaland, is born!

211
00:15:23,300 --> 00:15:28,220
Plus, the moat has a flowing hot spring,

212
00:15:28,220 --> 00:15:31,700
and inside the castle,
a grand banquet hall and a souvenir shop.

213
00:15:33,220 --> 00:15:36,980
During the show, there's a Polynesian
dance by ninjas and palace maids.

214
00:15:36,980 --> 00:15:41,020
The Tenshikaku is actually a karaoke venue.

215
00:15:41,020 --> 00:15:44,640
You can feel like a true Torosama,
singing with the Torosama Kings.

216
00:15:44,640 --> 00:15:48,960
And the pièce de résistance:
a golden shachihoko coat check.

217
00:15:48,960 --> 00:15:50,560
This is pretty luxurious, you know.

218
00:15:50,560 --> 00:15:53,080
Well, that's about it.

219
00:15:53,580 --> 00:15:56,520
Wow, that's amazing, senpai.
It's a huge project!

220
00:15:56,520 --> 00:15:57,420
Really?

221
00:15:58,060 --> 00:16:01,360
B-but senpai,
where are you going to get the land?

222
00:16:01,700 --> 00:16:03,760
There's no piece of land that big, you know.

223
00:16:03,760 --> 00:16:04,800
Y-yeah, that's right.

224
00:16:04,800 --> 00:16:08,020
You're not planning to tear down Kameari Park,
are you?

225
00:16:08,020 --> 00:16:09,520
That's exactly it.

226
00:16:09,520 --> 00:16:11,960
A hot spring for the residents,
by the residents.

227
00:16:11,960 --> 00:16:15,900
We'll have the park land
donated to this Hashutsujo Onsen.

228
00:16:15,900 --> 00:16:17,040
Eeeh?!

229
00:16:18,520 --> 00:16:20,080
But that's beside the point.

230
00:16:20,080 --> 00:16:21,740
we won't get permission.

231
00:16:22,660 --> 00:16:25,020
We'll make the press our allies.

232
00:16:25,020 --> 00:16:26,200
The press...

233
00:16:26,200 --> 00:16:29,140
We've already set the date
for the press coverage.

234
00:16:29,140 --> 00:16:32,160
Leave everything to me.

235
00:16:40,640 --> 00:16:43,340
Well, is the hot spring's
water volume going to increase?

236
00:16:44,100 --> 00:16:45,760
Can't say yet.

237
00:16:45,760 --> 00:16:49,320
To turn the police box hot
spring into a giant leisure land,

238
00:16:49,320 --> 00:16:51,620
we need to increase the water volume.

239
00:16:51,620 --> 00:16:52,820
Count on you.

240
00:16:53,480 --> 00:16:53,880
Yes.

241
00:17:19,400 --> 00:17:22,040
What? The hot spring stopped flowing?

242
00:17:22,440 --> 00:17:24,600
Even with the valve fully open,
it's no good.

243
00:17:25,100 --> 00:17:26,680
Let me try.

244
00:17:30,900 --> 00:17:33,440
It's no use, it's already full.

245
00:17:35,280 --> 00:17:39,280
Damn it, the press is coming tomorrow!

246
00:17:39,840 --> 00:17:41,300
We're completely screwed

247
00:17:41,300 --> 00:17:43,400
We can't give up now, not after all this.

248
00:17:43,860 --> 00:17:46,320
Listen,
this whole area has the same bedrock.

249
00:17:46,320 --> 00:17:50,240
If we dig here and there,
digging like crazy, we're bound to hit it.

250
00:17:50,240 --> 00:17:52,500
The hot spring will definitely come out.

251
00:17:58,580 --> 00:18:00,440
Well? Did it come out?

252
00:18:00,960 --> 00:18:02,880
This side's no good.

253
00:18:02,880 --> 00:18:05,440
Nothing at all, it's no good, senpai.

254
00:18:05,440 --> 00:18:08,440
Don't give up!
Keep digging until it comes out.

255
00:18:08,440 --> 00:18:09,240
Yes.

256
00:18:09,240 --> 00:18:13,320
Alright, one more push!

257
00:18:27,120 --> 00:18:27,660
Aaaaaah!

258
00:18:27,660 --> 00:18:30,800
Eeeeeeeh!

259
00:18:36,540 --> 00:18:39,120
The rock is too hard, it won't crack!

260
00:18:41,280 --> 00:18:44,960
Something smells weird, like gas.

261
00:18:45,420 --> 00:18:47,300
It's too dark, I can't see anything.

262
00:18:53,500 --> 00:18:55,560
You broke the gas canister, didn't you!

263
00:18:58,720 --> 00:19:00,420
Like I thought, nothing's coming out.

264
00:19:00,420 --> 00:19:02,160
What do we do, Ryotsu?

265
00:19:02,160 --> 00:19:03,860
We cover it up.

266
00:19:03,860 --> 00:19:09,620
Cover it up? How are we supposed to
bring in a boiler and heat the water?

267
00:19:10,180 --> 00:19:16,060
Will that really cover it up? After that, we'll
just manage somehow under the hot spring, yeah.

268
00:19:16,060 --> 00:19:17,360
How would I know!

269
00:19:22,080 --> 00:19:27,920
We're done. We pulled an all-nighter.
It's already morning.

270
00:19:29,680 --> 00:19:33,020
Listen, we have to get through
today's press coverage no matter what.

271
00:19:33,640 --> 00:19:38,340
Got it, Honda?
Add this bath essence every 30 minutes.

272
00:19:38,920 --> 00:19:41,700
Am I doing this alone? I'm so sleepy.

273
00:19:42,100 --> 00:19:45,300
I've got to deal with the press, too.

274
00:19:45,300 --> 00:19:47,480
Sakonji is on massage duty.

275
00:19:48,620 --> 00:19:53,140
Got it? I'll bring a thermos for
the rice balls and miso soup later.

276
00:19:53,140 --> 00:19:54,620
Understood.

277
00:19:59,300 --> 00:20:06,340
On today's Machikado Watching, we report on the Hashutsujo Onsen
that has sprung up at the popular Kameari Kōen-mae Hashutsujo.

278
00:20:07,280 --> 00:20:08,500
It's starting.

279
00:20:08,500 --> 00:20:10,560
Then let's head over to Afron.

280
00:20:11,440 --> 00:20:13,680
Because it's important work, Sakura, too.

281
00:20:16,060 --> 00:20:20,840
This is Sergeant Ryotsu, the man
who struck the police box hot spring.

282
00:20:21,220 --> 00:20:22,220
Ryotsu here.

283
00:20:23,020 --> 00:20:26,960
Ryotsu, how did you strike
this police box hot spring?

284
00:20:27,760 --> 00:20:30,560
Well, it was in preparation for Tokyo's water shortage,
you see.

285
00:20:30,560 --> 00:20:34,200
I thought I'd dig a well
for the local residents.

286
00:20:35,060 --> 00:20:37,660
And then hot spring water came gushing out,
is that right?

287
00:20:38,280 --> 00:20:41,420
Yes, I think God must have given it to us.

288
00:20:41,880 --> 00:20:44,240
Unbelievable, listen to him saying that.

289
00:20:44,240 --> 00:20:46,200
As expected of a senior officer.

290
00:20:46,760 --> 00:20:51,500
I hear there's also a plan to redevelop
Kameari Park into a leisure land.

291
00:20:52,160 --> 00:20:57,260
Yes, we're doing our very best so
we can meet the residents' requests.

292
00:20:57,960 --> 00:21:01,580
Well then, let's have Ryotsu
show us the hot spring right away.

293
00:21:01,580 --> 00:21:03,720
Yes, this way, please.

294
00:21:04,880 --> 00:21:06,000
Excuse me.

295
00:21:15,240 --> 00:21:17,860
This is the men's outdoor bath.

296
00:21:18,440 --> 00:21:21,000
Now let's hear what the customers think.

297
00:21:21,500 --> 00:21:22,960
Hey, hey, hey, hey!

298
00:21:25,350 --> 00:21:28,820
Right! We have to add
the hot spring essence!

299
00:21:31,260 --> 00:21:33,160
I can't sleep!

300
00:21:33,160 --> 00:21:35,580
Aaaaaah!

301
00:21:36,940 --> 00:21:37,500
Mm.

302
00:21:43,300 --> 00:21:54,160
How is this hot spring?
It's really wonderful, thank you.

303
00:21:57,340 --> 00:21:58,200
And you?

304
00:21:58,860 --> 00:22:02,500
Seaweed is floating in it too,
and the water is just like miso soup.

305
00:22:05,160 --> 00:22:06,860
Seaweed? Miso soup?

306
00:22:07,040 --> 00:22:08,660
That idiot...

307
00:22:10,320 --> 00:22:12,440
It even smells like miso soup, doesn't it?

308
00:22:12,900 --> 00:22:16,460
What is this? Weird water,
and something weird is floating in it!

309
00:22:21,520 --> 00:22:23,500
This really is miso soup!

310
00:22:24,160 --> 00:22:25,140
Tofu is floating up!

311
00:22:28,340 --> 00:22:30,340
Ryo-san, what is this?

312
00:22:30,640 --> 00:22:31,280
Th-that's right!

313
00:22:31,520 --> 00:22:34,060
A miso soup hot spring,
like no other in the world!

314
00:22:34,300 --> 00:22:37,220
Red miso, white miso,
mixed miso, just kidding!

315
00:22:40,400 --> 00:22:41,460
Ryotsu!

316
00:22:44,920 --> 00:22:46,240
Honda, you bastard!

317
00:22:46,660 --> 00:22:48,100
S-sorry, s-sorry!

318
00:22:48,860 --> 00:22:51,100
Ryotsu! This idiot!

319
00:22:51,100 --> 00:22:54,560
So the hot spring coming
up was a lie from the start

320
00:22:54,560 --> 00:22:58,220
No, it really was a hot spring at first!

321
00:22:58,220 --> 00:22:59,580
Good quote, that.

322
00:22:59,580 --> 00:23:03,680
The leisure land plan was a lie too,
you know.

323
00:23:03,680 --> 00:23:05,780
We're in trouble now...

324
00:23:05,780 --> 00:23:07,680
Please believe me!

325
00:23:07,680 --> 00:23:08,460
Seriously?

326
00:23:08,480 --> 00:23:09,040
Seriously?

327
00:23:20,080 --> 00:23:20,960
W-what?

328
00:23:25,020 --> 00:23:25,780
Hot!

329
00:23:26,260 --> 00:23:27,740
D-Dad, look at this!

330
00:23:29,140 --> 00:23:31,800
It's a hot spring!
A hot spring has sprung up!

331
00:23:32,380 --> 00:23:35,500
With this, we can make it!
A hot spring bathhouse!

332
00:23:36,140 --> 00:23:39,040
Everyone will come back to us now, Dad!

333
00:23:39,240 --> 00:23:41,420
Yes, this is wonderful news!

334
00:23:44,320 --> 00:23:46,800
It really was a hot spring at first,
you know!

335
00:23:48,960 --> 00:23:51,020
Please treat me to something.

336
00:23:51,720 --> 00:23:53,040
Idiot!

337
00:23:53,040 --> 00:24:00,040
Why is it always the
ping-pong lottery for me?

338
00:24:14,520 --> 00:24:17,140
Summer has come again this year.

339
00:24:19,920 --> 00:24:23,040
Summer has come again this year.

340
00:24:25,220 --> 00:24:28,580
On the big road, drink it all, yajuku-no.

341
00:24:28,580 --> 00:24:34,520
With a big chest, chest-juku-no, yajuku-no.

342
00:24:34,520 --> 00:24:40,960
Summer has come again this year.

343
00:24:43,660 --> 00:24:46,840
Summer has come again this year.

344
00:24:49,160 --> 00:24:52,300
Big waves, small waves,
tiny little ones, about that size.

345
00:24:52,300 --> 00:24:55,180
In the southern breeze, hoi.

346
00:24:55,180 --> 00:24:58,420
Big bottoms, small bottoms,
tiny little ones, about that size.

347
00:24:58,420 --> 00:24:59,680
On the shore.

348
00:24:59,680 --> 00:25:02,880
Buri buri buri buri buri buri buri buri
buri buri buri buri buri buri buri buri

349
00:25:02,880 --> 00:25:08,420
In the southern breeze, hoi.

350
00:25:12,200 --> 00:25:14,400
In the southern breeze, hoi.

351
00:25:17,700 --> 00:25:18,420
On the shore.

352
00:25:18,540 --> 00:25:20,020
Poro poro, wave slope, yo.

353
00:25:20,020 --> 00:25:22,180
Poro poro, poro poro, poro poro.

354
00:25:22,180 --> 00:25:23,480
Pocho.

355
00:25:29,560 --> 00:25:31,860
What? Another robot cop?

356
00:25:31,860 --> 00:25:34,300
This time he'd better
actually be useful, right?

357
00:25:34,300 --> 00:25:35,580
Whoa, don't get angry!

358
00:25:35,580 --> 00:25:36,320
Whoa, wh-whoa!

359
00:25:36,320 --> 00:25:38,260
So he bursts into flames when he gets angry?

360
00:25:38,260 --> 00:25:40,120
What a dangerous bastard.

361
00:25:40,120 --> 00:25:41,160
Alright, it's decided!

362
00:25:41,160 --> 00:25:42,360
Your name is...

363
00:25:42,360 --> 00:25:43,980
Doikari Honoo-no-suke!

364
00:25:43,980 --> 00:25:46,900
Next time: "The Blazing Robot Cop!"

365
00:25:46,900 --> 00:25:47,860
Nice to meet you.

366
00:25:48,620 --> 00:25:50,940
That place is Kameary!

367
00:25:52,040 --> 00:25:54,320
Yeah, it's definitely Kameary!

368
00:25:54,320 --> 00:25:59,300
Come on over to our town, everyone!

369
00:26:00,360 --> 00:26:00,880
Thank you.

